Think: Extract all integer substrings from each file in 'files' and write them (one per match) into temp_workspace/numbers_<original_filename>.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  fname=FILENAME; sub(".*/","",fname);
  out="temp_workspace/numbers_" fname ".txt";
  line=$0;
  while(match(line, /[+-]?[0-9]+/)) {
    print substr(line, RSTART, RLENGTH) >> out;
    line = substr(line, RSTART+RLENGTH);
  }
}' files/*
